**Lesson** — *Format datasetu YOLO i data.yaml* (module `m3`, 13 min, Polish prose with English technical terms, balanced 0.5 theory/practice). Six sections, no two theory back-to-back, ends on a widget:
1. **theory** `struktura` (176 words) — the two parallel `images/`/`labels/` trees, basename pairing, train/val/test, empty-`.txt` background images. Inline schematic image.
2. **plotImage** `normalizacja` — a 640×480 box figure with **real pixel axes/labels/title/grid**, showing rogi → środek+rozmiar → znormalizowane `0 0.5 0.65 0.4 0.3`. `sourceCode` is the exact script that rendered the PNG.
3. **quiz** `check-normalizacja` — distractors are the two canonical dataset bugs (pixels vs normalized, corners vs center), with a worked arithmetic explanation.
4. **theory** `linia-i-datayaml` (213 words) — the `class cx cy w h` row, KaTeX normalization equations, full `data.yaml` (`path/train/val/test/nc/names`), and the `nc == len(names)` rule. Inline annotated label-line image.
5. **code** `cwiczenie-voc-yolo` — implement `voc_to_yolo(...)` (VOC pixel corners → YOLO normalized center/size); 4 tests (1 visible smoke + 3 hidden), full `solution`. Verified all tests pass.
6. **sandbox** `piaskownica` — assemble a `data.yaml`, parse a label line, convert back to pixels.
**Assets generated locally** (no external URLs anywhere): `assets/plots/format-datasetu-yolo-i-datayaml-1.png` + `assets/images/{struktura-datasetu-yolo,linia-etykiety-yolo}.png`, all rendered via Bash and visually verified.
**Sources** — 4 entries (2 Ultralytics docs articles + VOC 2010 and COCO 2014 papers with author/year), plus section-level sources on both theory beats.
